     7	## Original decisions (handoff, Sept 2026)
     8	
     9	| # | Decision | Why | Rejected alternative |
    10	|---|---|---|---|
    11	| 1 | Weekly 20-hr cap counts **booked** hours | Members need to see what's left *before* booking, and booking is the only moment the limit can be enforced. | Counting checked-in hours: it's only known after the fact, so it's too late to stop anyone. |
    12	| 2 | Check-in makes a booking real; no check-in by +30 min **releases it and returns the hours** | Keeps the numbers honest and frees busy spots without punishing anyone. | Penalties for no-shows. |
    13	| 3 | **No required sign-out.** Auto check-out happens at the booked end time; "Still here?" offers an extension | A required sign-out feels like clocking in and out, and people forget. | Manual check-out required. |
    14	| 4 | "I'm wrapping up" means finishing **on time**, so no hours are returned. Only **Check out early** returns hours | Christie: tapping "wrapping up" means leaving on time, not early. | Returning the 10 minutes left when they tap. |
    15	| 5 | "Still here?" appears **10 min** before the end, with **30 min / 1 / 1.5 / 2 hr** choices plus a "Book more time" link | Staying longer should be one tap. 5 minutes is too tight when someone's mid-glaze. | Sending members to the Book page to extend. |
    16	| 6 | Capacity is a **guideline**: booking is always allowed, the real count is shown even when over (e.g., "5 booked for 4"), and another area is suggested | Christie's call. Blocking frustrates members, and the over-count data supports future equipment decisions. | Hard capacity limits. |
    17	| 7 | Members book **an area, never a specific station**. No station numbers appear anywhere | Skedda let members book specific spots, which led to "I booked this spot" conflicts. There's nothing to point at if no number is shown. | Numbered stations, or a separate standing-wheel category. |
    18	| 8 | Standing wheels are **part of Wheels** | Avoids ownership over specific wheels. | A separate category. |
    19	| 9 | Members see **counts, never names**, for both bookings and RSVPs. **AMENDED Sep 27 by #45:** the in-studio front-door tablet shows a first-name list of who's here now and arriving soon. Everywhere else, counts only. | Showing names would reveal each other's schedules. Counts give members everything they need to plan. | A list of who's booked or going. |
    20	| 10 | **No messaging.** "Notify everyone going" is a one-way notice | Two-way messaging is a big build and the place bugs pile up. Ask Clay Hub covers questions. | An in-app chat or inbox for replies. |
    21	| 11 | **No email** from the app beyond Firebase sign-in links | It would mean adding a separate email service, which is more setup and more that can break. | Email as a backup for urgent notices. |
    22	| 12 | **Inbox first, push later.** The inbox works for everyone regardless of push settings. **PARTLY SUPERSEDED Sep 27 by #46:** push to the two *staff* phones (for no-show alerts) comes in Phase 1. Push to *members* stays later (Phase 4), and the inbox still comes first for members. | Push, especially on iPhone, is the fussiest part of the stack. Each phone must allow push itself, and the app can't force it. | Push in Phase 1. |
    23	| 13 | Inbox keeps **2 weeks**, and the screen says so | Enough to catch missed items, short enough to stay tidy. The activity log is separate and kept forever. | Keeping the inbox forever. |
    24	| 14 | The unread signal is a **bell count on the Feed plus a dot on the Feed tab**. **AMENDED Sep 27 by #51:** the dot is **orange** (pink is reserved for cancelled/changes, DESIGN.md). | Visible from every screen without adding a sixth tab. | A Notifications tab. |
    25	| 15 | Missed-check-in notices are **one card that updates in place** (reminder → last call → released) | Avoids stacking three notices for one booking. | Three separate notifications. |
    26	| 16 | QR scan checks in **automatically** when booked; when not booked it goes to open spots. **AMENDED Sep 27 by #47:** scanning (or tapping Check in) *more than 15 minutes early* offers two one-tap "Start now" choices instead of checking in. | Fewest taps. | A confirm button after scanning. |
    27	| 17 | The kiosk handles **walk-in booking**, and its copy never mentions asking staff | Members can do everything on the tablet. Christie removed the Studio Tech wording. | "Book in the app first, then come back." |
