     1	# My Clay Hub — Product Spec
     2	
     3	Version 2.0 · Sep 27, 2026 · owner: Christie. (v1.0 was the "Clay Hub Members" handoff.)
     4	
     5	- **Decisions:** numbers in the form #N refer to `DECISIONS.md`.
     6	- **Data:** `DATA-MODEL.md` has the collections and server functions.
     7	- **Plan:** `~/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html` is the foundation plan.
     8	- **Mockups:** screen numbers in parentheses, like (05), match `design-reference/screens/NN-*.png`. They're for **layout only**. Colours, fonts and copy come from this spec and `DESIGN.md`.
     9	
    10	---
    11	
    12	## 1. What this is
    13	
    14	**My Clay Hub** is a member-facing app for **Clay Hub** members to:
    15	
    16	- book studio time (replacing Skedda),
    17	- check in and out, so staff know who's in the studio,
    18	- see studio news (firing photos, updates) in a one-way feed,
    19	- see what's on (weekly schedule, events, changes, reminders),
    20	- get notified about things that affect them.
    21	
    22	It also has staff tools, in the `/staff` section, to see today's studio, catch no-shows, post, manage events and changes, and see usage reports.
    23	
    24	**Not** Membership Manager. Membership Manager stays the system of record for members. My Clay Hub gets a **one-way copy** of just the fields it needs through a live link (§3), and never writes back.
    25	
    26	It lives in **its own Firebase project, `my-clay-hub`**, separate from `tinker-hq-apps` where every internal staff app lives (#30).
    27	
    28	**North star: it must work without bugs.** When in doubt, choose the simpler behavior. Don't add features that aren't in this spec.
    29	
    30	---
    31	
    32	## 2. People and access
    33	
    34	### Members
    35	- Sign in with **email magic link** or **Google** (01). No passwords.
    36	- After sign-in, the app checks the membership (#33). The member must match **exactly one** live Membership Manager record by verified email, with a status that allows sign-in: **active**, **paused** or **review** (see §3).
    37	- Anyone else sees: "We couldn't find a Clay Hub membership for this email. Try the email address the studio has on file for you. Questions? clayhub@tinkerartstudio.com"
    38	- Magic-link emails are sent by Firebase Auth itself. The app sends **no other email**.
    39	- Stays signed in on their phone.
    40	
    41	### Staff
    42	- Staff don't get a second password. They sign in to My Clay Hub's **`/staff`** section with their existing **Tinker HQ login**. Tinker HQ has a tile that opens it (#31).
    43	- Access comes from Tinker HQ's **Manage Team**, with a new access box, **`my-clay-hub`**:
    44	  - **Staff with the box ticked** (**Maryssa**, the People & Operations coordinator, **and the studio tech**: two people): today's bookings and who's checked in, no-show alerts and "check in for them", post to the feed (12), post changes, manage events (15), and **reports and CSV downloads (14)** (#50).
    45	  - **Managers and admins** (automatically, by role): everything above, plus **settings** (spaces, capacities, hours, cap, timings, kilns, links).
    46	- **To remove someone's staff access**, untick them (or make them inactive) in Manage Team. It takes effect within a minute. Disabling their Tinker HQ login alone doesn't remove it (#31).
    47	- Staff can post from a phone (composer 12 is phone-sized) and from desktop.
    48	
    49	### Front-door tablet (kiosk, 13)
    50	- A dedicated device signed in with its own **kiosk** account in `my-clay-hub` (#39). It can check people in, create walk-in bookings, and show the "Here now / Arriving soon" first-name list (§6, #45). It can never browse member data.
    51	
    52	---
    53	
    54	## 3. Membership Manager integration (one-way link, separate project)
    55	
    56	My Clay Hub doesn't read Membership Manager's collection directly: it's in a different Firebase project. A small function next to Membership Manager watches for changes and **re-sends a snapshot** of each changed member into My Clay Hub, usually within a minute. A check every 6 hours repairs anything missed (#53). Nothing is ever written back (#37).
    57	
    58	**Fields copied:** name (first name and last initial are worked out from it), email, Membership Manager's status (`stage`), pause dates, last day, member-since (#36), and the **last 4 digits** of the cell phone (#24). Full phone numbers never leave Membership Manager's project.
    59	
    60	**Member status** is worked out by one tested function from the **dates**, with Membership Manager's `stage` as a backstop, because `stage` is only brought up to date when someone opens Membership Manager (#34). The full rule order is in `DATA-MODEL.md`.
    61	
    62	| Status | What happens in My Clay Hub |
    63	|---|---|
    64	| **Active** | Can sign in and use everything. Newly activated members are covered automatically: they just sign in with their email. No manual setup, and no invite email from this app. |
    65	| **Paused** | Can sign in and see the Feed, What's on and My time. **Booking is locked** (06): "Your membership is paused through [end date]. You can still see the feed and what's on. Booking opens back up on [end date + 1]." **The pause end date is the last paused day** (#35): a pause of Jan 2 – Feb 1 means booking reopens Feb 2. Bookings inside the pause window are **cancelled automatically** when the pause is set, and each cancellation writes an inbox notice. |
    66	| **Review** | The membership record has a gap or an inconsistency (for example a pause with no end date). Can sign in and see the feed. **Booking is locked** with "We're checking your membership details — you can still see the feed." Staff see a flag to fix the record in Membership Manager. |
    67	| **Offboarded** | From the day **after** their last day (the last day itself still has access): sign-in is turned off (the account is disabled, **not deleted**) and future bookings are cancelled. All history stays in reports. If they're reactivated later, access and history come back. |
    68	| **Not yet / Removed** | Onboarding or touring members, and records no longer live in Membership Manager, can't sign in. |
    69	
    70	Status changes made in Membership Manager take effect automatically. Staff never update two systems. A **pause request that Membership Manager hasn't processed yet** (a Quick Log request) doesn't lock booking until it's processed (#70). When a member is **removed**, My Clay Hub keeps their name and dates for history but drops their email and phone digits (#71). When a member's email changes, Membership Manager keeps their permanent member ID, so their bookings and history carry over (#52).
    71	
    72	---
    73	
    74	## 4. Studio setup (all editable by managers and admins in Settings, not hard-coded)
    75	
    76	### Areas and capacity
    77	| Area | Capacity | Notes |
    78	|---|---|---|
    79	| Glaze station | **4** | |
    80	| Wheels | **10** | Includes 2 standing wheels. They are **not** a separate category. |
    81	| Handbuilding table | **6** | |
    82	
    83	Members book **time in an area, never a specific station**. The UI must never show station numbers (#7).
    84	
    85	### Open hours (America/Denver time)
    86	- Opens **5:00 AM** daily.
    87	- Closing time is a **per-weekday setting**, **11:00 PM every night at launch**. Managers may later set any night except Tuesday to **12:00 AM (midnight)**. **Tuesday is fixed at 11:00 PM** because cleaners arrive at 11 (#27). The late-night usage report (§11) informs that decision.
    88	- Holiday or one-off closures are posted as a **Change** (§9).
    89	
    90	### Kilns
    91	- Two kilns: **Hestia** and **Lumi** (Lumi is the larger oval kiln). Refer to them **by name only**, with no descriptions in the member UI.
    92	- Store kilns as an editable list (name only), so one can be added or renamed without code.
    93	- The app does **not** track live kiln status (#18).
    94	
    95	### Weekly cap
    96	- **20 hours per member per week.** The week runs **from Monday 00:00 to the next Monday 00:00, America/Denver** (so a Sunday booking ending at 12:00 AM counts in full). The cap is a setting.
    97	
    98	---
    99	
   100	## 5. Booking (05, 06)
   101	
   102	### Creating a booking
   103	- **Day:** today plus the next 13 days (**14 days**, a setting) (#49). They're shown as two rows of day chips.
   104	- **Start time:** a dropdown in **15-minute steps**, from 5:00 AM to the last 15 minutes before close (#48).
   105	- **How long:** chips for **1h to 6h**. Each chip shows the length on top and the **end time** underneath ("3h / 9:00"), in the same two-line style as the day chips. Chips that would run past closing are disabled, with both lines crossed out.
   106	- **"Other end time":** a small link under the chips. It opens an end-time dropdown in 15-minute steps, for in-between lengths (up to 6 hours). When it's used, the chips deselect and a line shows the length ("2 h 45 min").
   107	- A line shows "Studio closes at 11:00 PM." On Tuesdays it adds "— cleaners come in."
   108	- **Where you'll work** (area). Under the area picker, always show: "Your booking saves you time in this area — not a specific station. Grab any open one when you arrive."
   109	
   110	### Capacity is a guideline, not a wall (#6)
   111	- The app counts how many bookings overlap the chosen window in that area and shows the **real number, even when it's over capacity**. It always shows the count against the total.
   112	- Three states:
   113	  - **Room to spare** (under 75% booked): "2 of 4 glaze stations booked for this window."
   114	  - **Getting busy** (75% or more).
   115	  - **Pretty full** (at or over capacity): "5 people booked for 4 glaze stations at this time. You can still book, but expect to share or wait. Handbuilding tables have room, or try an earlier time." Plus a one-tap **"Switch to [other area]"** button.
   116	- Booking is **always allowed**, regardless of capacity.
   117	
   118	### Weekly hours are the one hard limit (#1)
   119	- Hours are counted from **bookings**, not usage, in minutes, and shown in quarter hours.
   120	- A meter shows the week the chosen day falls in: "This week (Mon–Sun): 15 of 20 hrs", then "Next week" and "Week of Oct 13" for later weeks. A preview line: "After this booking: 17¾ of 20 hrs · 2¼ left".
   121	- If a booking would go over the cap, the button is disabled and reads **"Over your weekly hours"**, with this explanation: "This would put you at 21 of 20 hrs. Shorten the session or pick a day in another week."
   122	
   123	### Changing or cancelling
   124	- Members can cancel a future booking from My time. The hours go back immediately. **There's no cancellation cutoff**: late cancels are welcome, because a no-show releases at +30 anyway.
   125	
   126	---
   127	
   128	## 6. Check-in lifecycle (the heart of the app)
   129	
   130	Every booking moves through these states, and **every transition is written to the activity log** (§12):
   131	
   132	```
   133	booked → checked_in → checked_out
   134	booked → cancelled            (by member, or by the system during a pause or offboarding)
   135	booked → released             (no check-in by start + 30 min)
   136	checked_in → extended → checked_out
   137	```
   138	
   139	### Ways to check in
   140	1. **QR code at the front door (13).** Scanning it opens the app to a check-in link.
   141	   - If they have a booking right now (from 15 minutes before its start), they're **checked in instantly, with no extra tap**, and land on "You're checked in" (10).
   142	   - If their booking starts **more than 15 minutes from now**, they see **"Start now"** (below).
   143	   - If they have no booking, they go to the Book screen showing open spots for right now.
   144	   - If they're not signed in, they sign in first, then continue the same way.
   145	2. **Front-door tablet (13):** enter the last 4 digits of their phone.
   146	   - Booked right now: checked in.
   147	   - Not booked: the tablet offers open spots right now, they book, and they're checked in, all on the tablet.
   148	   - If two members share the same last 4 digits, the tablet shows each one's first name and last initial ("Sam R." / "Sam T."), and the member taps theirs.
   149	3. **In the app:** the "Check in" button on the Feed session card (02), on My time (08), or on the reminder notification (03). It's honor-system, since it works from anywhere. Accepted.
   150	4. **Staff:** "They're here: check in" from a no-show alert (below).
   151	
   152	- The **check-in window** opens **15 minutes before start**.
   153	- Tablet copy: "Scan with your phone to check in" (with a small line under it: "Not booked? It'll take you to open spots.") and "Or enter the last 4 of your phone to check in". There is **no** "ask the Studio Tech" wording anywhere.
   154	
   155	### Arriving early: "Start now" (#47)
   156	Checking in more than 15 minutes before the booked start shows: "Your session starts at 6:00 PM. Start now instead?" with two one-tap choices:
   157	- **Start now, same length:** the booking moves earlier and ends earlier. No change in hours.
   158	- **Start now, keep my end time:** the extra time is added and counts toward the weekly cap like an extension. It's disabled if it would go over the cap or past closing.
   159	
   160	Both show the area's current count, and both write an activity-log entry.
   161	
   162	### Kiosk "Here now / Arriving soon" list (#45)
   163	The front-door tablet shows members whose booking is live right now, from 15 minutes before start until the booked end:
   164	- **Here now:** checked in.
   165	- **Arriving soon:** in the window, not checked in yet.
   166	
   167	It shows **first names only**. When two people on the list share a first name, both get a last initial ("Katie M.", "Katie S."). If the initials match too, the first two letters of the last name are used. It doesn't show the area. The list is **display-only**: tapping a name does nothing. (An optional "hide my name on the studio tablet" setting may come later.)
   168	
   169	### Missed check-in: reminder → last call → released (03, 04)
   170	All three are the **same inbox card updating in place**, not three separate notifications (#15).
   171	
   172	| When | Card | Actions |
   173	|---|---|---|
   174	| Start + **10 min**, not checked in | "Session started · Your 6:00 PM glaze station session started. Made it? Check in so we know you're here. Change of plans? Cancel and your hours go back." | **I'm here · check in** / **Cancel booking** |
   175	| Start + **20 min** | "Last call · Your glaze station releases at 6:30 PM. Still coming? Check in to keep your spot. If not, cancel and your 3 hours go back to your week." | same two buttons |
   176	| Start + **30 min** | "Booking released · You didn't check in, so we released your 6:00 PM glaze station. Your 3 hours are back — you have 8 left this week. Still want to come in? Book an open spot." | **Book an open spot** (the other buttons disappear) |
   177	
   178	A released booking frees its capacity and returns its hours to the weekly total.
   179	
   180	### Staff no-show alert (#46)
   181	At **last call (+20 min)**, staff with the `my-clay-hub` box get a **no-show alert**, for no-shows only; nothing is sent for ordinary bookings or check-ins.
   182	- It reads "Sam R. · Glaze · booked 6:00 PM · not checked in", with **"They're here: check in"** (checks them in as `staff`, and the booking isn't released) or **"Not here"** (dismiss; release happens at +30 as normal).
   183	- It appears in a panel at the top of the staff Today view, with a badge, and a chime while the screen is open.
   184	- It's also sent as a **push notification to the staff member's phone** (Phase 1, set up in person on Maryssa's and the studio tech's phones).
   185	- Each staff member can turn alerts on or off for themselves.
   186	
   187	### During the session
   188	- **"You're checked in" (10):** shows the area, arrival time and booked-until time. Copy: "Have a great session. At 8:50 PM we'll ask if you want to stay longer — otherwise you're checked out at 9:00." Also a **Check out early** button, and any current Change alert as a heads-up.
   189	
   190	### End of session: "Still here?" (11)
   191	- Shown **10 minutes before the booked end** (a setting; the other allowed value is 5).
   192	- Extension choices: **30 min / 1 hr / 1.5 hr / 2 hr**. The default is 30 min. Each choice shows its new end time, and the button reads "Stay until 9:30 PM".
   193	- Choices that would run past **closing time** are disabled and labeled "closed", with the note "Studio closes at 11:00 PM on Tuesdays — cleaners come in."
   194	- Choices that would go over the **weekly cap** are disabled.
   195	- Helper text shows availability: "Glaze station is open until 9:30 PM. Leaves you 4½ hours this week."
   196	- If the area is at or over capacity for the extension window, they **can still stay in the same area**. Show the real count and *suggest* another area: "All 4 glaze stations are booked after 9:00 PM. You can still stay — or move to a handbuilding table, which has room." (#6)
   197	- **"I'm wrapping up"** means finishing **on time** (#4). It shows "Thanks for coming in! Sounds good. We'll check you out at 9:00 PM — no need to do anything else." **No hours are returned.**
   198	- A **"Book more time"** link goes to Book for anything longer.
   199	- With no response, the member is **automatically checked out at the booked end time**.
   200	- If the session already ends at closing time, skip the "Still here?" prompt. Show "Studio closes at [time] — time to wrap up" 10 minutes before close instead.
   201	- An extension counts toward the weekly cap exactly like a booking.
   202	
   203	### Leaving early
   204	- **Check out early** (on screen 10) is the **only** way hours are returned for an in-progress session. Unused time is returned **rounded up to the next 15 minutes**, in the member's favour (#48).
   205	
   206	---
   207	
   208	## 7. Member screens
   209	
   210	Bottom tab bar on every main screen: **Feed · Book · What's on · My time · Profile**. When there are unread notifications, a small dot appears on the **Feed** tab.
   211	
   212	**02 Feed**
   213	- Header: the My Clay Hub wordmark (logo SVG, `DESIGN.md`), plus a **bell with an unread count** that opens Notifications (03).
   214	- A pinned **Change banner** at the top while any change is active ("Change today · No Office Hours tonight"). Tapping it opens What's on.
   215	- **Today's session card** (if booked today): time, area, and a **Check in** button.
   216	- **Posts**, newest first: author, time, type tag, text, and a photo grid showing up to 4 photos plus "+N more". One **"Love it"** reaction with a count. **No comments.**
   217	
   218	**03/04 Notifications (inbox)**
   219	- Reached from the Feed bell, from Profile ("See all notifications"), and, once member push exists (Phase 4), from a push notification.
   220	- Sections: **New** and **Earlier** ("Last 2 weeks"). Footer: "Notifications clear after 2 weeks. Your bookings and visits stay in My time."
   221	- The inbox works for everyone, whether or not push is enabled.
   222	- Opening the inbox clears the bell count and the tab dot.
   223	
   224	**05 Book / 06 Book (paused):** see §5 and §3.
   225	
   226	**07 What's on**
   227	- **Changes:** active change alerts, colour-coded by kind (cancelled, moved), each with the time it was posted.
   228	- **Every week (listed only, no RSVP, no reminder toggle):**
   229	  - Mon · Member Firing: glaze & bisque firings (never say which kiln does which, because they sometimes switch)
   230	  - Wed · Kiln unload: finished work on the pickup shelves
   231	  - **Office Hours with Julia (Fall 2026): Wednesdays 5–6 PM · Thursdays 12:45–1:45 PM.** These change every semester. Staff edit them in the Events screen (15), and can enter next semester's times ahead with "runs from / until" dates.
   232	  - If a weekly item is cancelled for a date, that row shows crossed out with an "Off today" tag.
   233	- **Coming up:** dated one-off events, like Member Happy Hour, with **I'm in** and **Add to calendar** (§8).
   234	- **Reminders:** standing rules, managed by staff:
   235	  - "Get work on the firing shelves by 9:30 AM Monday to make that week's Member Firing." (A soft guideline: work on the shelf when loading starts still goes in.)
   236	  - "Label every piece with your name before it goes on a kiln shelf."
   237	  - "Check in when you arrive — it keeps your hours accurate."
   238	  - Launch reminder: "Bookings hold studio time, not a specific station."
   239	- Each event type shows a small **pot illustration** as its icon (`DESIGN.md`). Christie sees mockups first.
   240	
   241	**08 My time**
   242	- A big weekly meter ("15 of 20 hours · 5 hours left · resets Monday"; quarter hours where needed).
   243	- **Upcoming:** bookings, with the current one highlighted and a Check in button, plus events they're going to.
   244	- **Recent visits:** checked in, or "Missed · hrs returned".
   245	
   246	**09 Profile**
   247	- Name, email and "Member since [date]", all from Membership Manager. If member-since is blank in Membership Manager, the line is hidden.
   248	- **Notifications:** until member push exists (Phase 4), this links to the inbox, with the line "Everything saves to your inbox."
   249	- **Questions or feedback?** An **Ask Clay Hub** button that opens https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd-RhLmSXsrlzow3JK7m0H77pEp3Gg5_zo0eKxNBBru1v0QoA/viewform in a new tab.
   250	- **Pause, cancel, or change your membership:** "Email us and we'll take care of it." with a mailto link to **clayhub@tinkerartstudio.com**. There's no in-app request flow.
   251	- **Sign out.**
   252	
   253	---
   254	
   255	## 8. Events and RSVPs
   256	
   257	There are two kinds of events:
   258	- **Recurring, listed only:** Office Hours, Member Firing, Kiln unload. No RSVP. Staff can **"Cancel a date"**, which crosses that date off in What's on **and automatically posts a Change alert**. Recurring items can have "runs from / until" dates.
   259	- **One-off with RSVP:** Member Happy Hour, workshops. There's an optional **spot cap**; when it's full, the event shows "Full".
   260	
   261	**Member side (07):**
   262	- Tapping **I'm in** turns the button area into a teal "success" card (DESIGN.md): "You're going · 12 members going. It's on your My time list. We'll remind you that afternoon, and let you know right away if anything changes."
   263	- The buttons then become **Add to calendar** and **Can't make it** (backs out in one tap).
   264	- Members see **counts only, never names**.
   265	- RSVPs do **not** count toward weekly hours.
   266	- An inbox reminder goes out on the day of the event (early afternoon).
   267	- If an event is edited, moved or cancelled, everyone going gets an inbox notice immediately.
   268	
   269	**Staff side (15, in `/staff`):**
   270	- Left column: upcoming RSVP events with their "N going" count; Every week (listed only), with **Cancel a date** and editable times and "runs from / until" dates; past events showing RSVP'd vs came vs walk-ins; and the **Reminders** lines for What's on (add, edit, reorder, remove).
   271	- The selected event shows **Going / Spots / Backed out** numbers; the **Who's going** list with names (staff only); and buttons for **Edit**, **Cancel or move**, **Notify everyone going** (sends an inbox notice, plus member push once it exists in Phase 4; **not** two-way messaging) and **Download list (CSV)**.
   272	- After the event, staff mark who came. This feeds the attendance report.
   273	- **+ New event** creates an event with: type (one-off or recurring), title, date or weekday, time, description, icon (pot), RSVP on/off, cap, and for recurring events optional "runs from / until" dates.
   274	
   275	---
   276	
   277	## 9. Posts and Changes (staff composer, 12)
   278	
   279	Post types:
   280	- **Firing photos:** text plus photos. Example: "This week's firing is out — look at all these beauties! Finished pieces are on the pickup shelves; look for your name tag."
   281	- **Studio update:** text, with photos optional.
   282	- **Schedule change:** creates a **Change alert**. It pins to the top of the Feed as a banner, appears under Changes in What's on, and sends an inbox notice to all members. It needs an **end date or time**, so it unpins automatically.
   283	
   284	The composer has a "Notify members" toggle for posts ("Sends to every member's notifications inbox"; member push is added in Phase 4). Change alerts always notify.
   285	
   286	Photos go to Firebase Storage in `my-clay-hub`. Resize them on upload.
   287	
   288	---
   289	
   290	## 10. Notifications
   291	
   292	- **Members: in-app inbox.** Every notification is a record in the member's inbox, with a bell count and tab dot. No email beyond sign-in links. No SMS.
   293	- **Staff: push in Phase 1** (#46), for no-show alerts only, on the two staff phones. Set up in person; on iPhone that means adding My Clay Hub to the Home Screen first.
   294	- **Members: push in Phase 4 (optional).** It uses Firebase Cloud Messaging. Ask for permission **after the member's first booking** ("Want a heads-up if your session changes?"), not on first launch. On iPhone, push only works after the member adds the app to their Home Screen, so show a short how-to. Push is always *in addition to* the inbox, never instead of it.
   295	- Inbox items expire after **14 days** (a Firestore TTL policy). The activity log is kept forever.
   296	
   297	Notification types (members):
   298	- check-in reminder, last call, released (all one card that updates in place, §6)
   299	- still here? (end of session)
   300	- booking cancelled by the system (pause or offboarding)
   301	- event reminder, event changed or cancelled
   302	- change alert
   303	- new post (if the staff member left "Notify" on)
   304	
   305	Notification types (staff): the no-show alert (§6).
   306	
   307	---
   308	
   309	## 11. Reports (14, in `/staff`; staff with the `my-clay-hub` box, managers and admins) (#50)
   310	
   311	- **Filters:** date range (Last 30 days / This month / Last 6 months / **All time** / Custom), and area.
   312	- **Summary numbers:** hours booked, hours used (checked in), check-in rate, no-shows, active members.
   313	- **"When the studio is busy" heatmap:** days of the week × hours from 5 AM to closing, showing the average number of people checked in.
   314	- **By area:** % booked; how often the area was at or over capacity (the count is shown even when over); how many "pretty full" warnings were shown, and how many members then switched area or time; sessions extended.
   315	- **Member table:** searchable. Columns: booked, used, check-in rate, no-shows, extended, average per week.
   316	- **Member detail panel:** a range picker (8 weeks / 6 months / **All time**); weekly bars against the 20-hr cap (weeks at the cap highlighted); usual area; usual time; check-in rate; member since; lifetime hours; **Export this member's history**.
   317	- **Downloads (CSV), all respecting the filters:**
   318	  1. **Full activity log:** every event, one row each, timestamped.
   319	  2. **Hourly occupancy:** the heatmap's raw data (date, hour, area, people checked in, spots booked).
   320	  3. **Member summary:** one row per member.
   321	  4. **Area summary:** one row per area per day.
   322	  5. **Events & RSVPs:** RSVPs vs attendance.
   323	- **Printable report:** a print-friendly page of the overview. This replaces the manual Skedda review.
   324	
   325	**Later reports (Phase 4+)**, all computed from the same activity log:
   326	- late-night (10–11 PM) and early (5–7 AM) usage, as input to the midnight and 5 AM decisions
   327	- demand vs capacity, by area and time
   328	- weekly cap pressure: how many members hit 20 hours, and how often
   329	- a drop-off list: members with no booking in 3+ weeks
   330	- app adoption: signed in, push enabled
   331	- event RSVP vs attendance trends
   332	- cancellation lead time
   333	- no-show alerts: how often staff found the person was actually there
   334	
   335	---
   336	
   337	## 12. Activity log (build first, keep forever)
   338	
   339	Every booking-related action is written as its **own immutable, timestamped record**. The booking is never simply overwritten. Record types:
   340	- booking created
   341	- cancelled (with who or what: member, pause, offboarding)
   342	- checked in (with the method: qr / kiosk / app / staff)
   343	- started early ("Start now", with the mode)
   344	- extended (with minutes)
   345	- checked out (with the reason: auto_end / early / wrapping_up)
   346	- released (no-show)
   347	- no-show alert sent (and how staff resolved it)
   348	- RSVP added or removed
   349	- event attendance marked
   350	
   351	Reports and CSVs are computed from this log. Nothing is ever deleted from it.
   352	
   353	**[Optional, Phase 4]** Import past Skedda exports into the log, so "All time" really is all time.
   354	
   355	---
   356	
   357	## 13. Security and privacy (non-negotiable)
   358	
   359	- **Members never get an account in `tinker-hq-apps`.** My Clay Hub is its own Firebase project, with its own rules. The only connection is the one-way link, which can read Membership Manager's records and can do nothing in My Clay Hub except call one private function (#30, #42).
   360	- Members can read **only their own** member fields, and **only their own** bookings, inbox and RSVPs.
   361	- Every member rule checks the member's **live status**, not just their sign-in claim. A pause or offboarding takes effect immediately (#33).
   362	- Capacity counts and RSVP counts are shown **without exposing who booked**. They're served from server-maintained aggregate docs or a Cloud Function. Clients can never query other members' bookings.
   363	- **No member ever sees another member's name in the app.** There are two exceptions, both on the in-studio kiosk:
   364	  - the same-last-4 tie-break (first name and last initial);
   365	  - the "Here now / Arriving soon" first-name list (#45).
   366	- **Full phone numbers never reach My Clay Hub.** Only the last 4 digits are copied (#24). No client can read them. Kiosk lookups go through a function that returns only candidate first name, last initial and booking status.
   367	- Staff screens are gated by the staff roster (from Manage Team) in both the UI and the Firestore rules, checked live.
   368	- Write **Firestore rules tests** (emulator) for every rule above before Phase 1 ships. The first test is "a signed-in stranger can do nothing".
   369	
   370	---
   371	
   372	## 14. Time-based jobs
   373	
   374	All of these run on the server (2nd-gen Cloud Functions, or Cloud Tasks), with **retries explicitly switched on**. They must be **idempotent**, meaning safe to run twice:
   375	- check-in reminder (+10 min), last call (+20 min, **plus the staff no-show alert**), release (+30 min)
   376	- still here? (end − 10 min), auto check-out at the end
   377	- closing-time wrap-up message
   378	- event-day reminder
   379	- pause set → cancel bookings in the pause window
   380	- offboarding: disable sign-in and cancel future bookings, from the day after the last day
   381	- member-status recompute: daily at **09:30 UTC** — 3:30 AM MDT / 2:30 AM MST, always after Denver midnight and before opening (#65)
   382	- the link's reconcile: every 6 hours
   383	- inbox TTL cleanup (a Firestore TTL policy)
   384	
   385	All member-facing times and calendar days are **America/Denver**. Scheduled jobs are *declared* in UTC (the functions guard allows only UTC), at times chosen to land in the right Denver window all year (#65). The tests must cover **DST changes** and **week boundaries**, for example a Sunday booking ending at 12:00 AM counts in that Sunday's week. No booking can cross midnight (DATA-MODEL.md, C6).
   386	
   387	`tinker-hq-apps` is on the **Blaze** plan. `my-clay-hub` will be created on Blaze in plan Phase D. Each project records its Firestore location, trigger location and function region (#54).
   388	
   389	---
   390	
   391	## 15. Build phases
   392	
   393	The foundation plan (`clayhub-members-foundation.html`) runs its own phases A–E first. This spec's phases map onto it like this:
   394	
   395	**Spec Phase 0 — Inspect and confirm (no app code): done.** This was plan Phase C, Sep 27, 2026. The existing systems were inspected, every open item was answered, and these docs were rewritten.
   396	
   397	**Before Phase 1 (plan phases A, B, D, D2, E):**
   398	- retire Clay Hub Booking;
   399	- make Membership Manager's saves reliable, fix its dates, and add a permanent member ID;
   400	- create the `my-clay-hub` project;
   401	- build a deploy guard for functions;
   402	- build the one-way link.
   403	
   404	**Spec Phase 1 — Book and check in (launch core); plan Phase F, its own plan:**
   405	- The Tinker HQ tile and Manage Team box; sign-in switched on (only now).
   406	- Member sign-in gated by membership status (§2, §3); paused, review and offboarded handling.
   407	- The staff login exchange; the minimal `/staff` Today view (today's bookings, who's checked in) with **no-show alerts and staff push**.
   408	- Settings: areas, capacities, hours, cap, timings.
   409	- Book (05/06) with soft capacity, the hard weekly cap, 15-minute times and the 14-day window.
   410	- My time (08).
   411	- Check-in: app, QR deep link, "Start now", and the kiosk tablet (13), including walk-in booking and the "Here now / Arriving soon" list.
   412	- Reminder → last call → release (03/04).
   413	- "Still here?" and extensions (11); auto check-out; check out early (10).
   414	- **Activity log.** Inbox (in-app). Profile (09).
   415	- Tests: hours math, capacity counts, lifecycle transitions, status derivation, time-zone and DST cases, Firestore rules.
   416	
   417	**Spec Phase 2 — Community**
   418	- Feed with posts, photos, and Love it (02).
   419	- Staff composer (12).
   420	- What's on (07): recurring listings (with semester dates), one-off events and RSVPs, Changes and the Feed banner, reminders, pot icons (mockups shown to Christie first).
   421	- Staff Events screen (15).
   422	
   423	**Spec Phase 3 — Reports**
   424	- Reports screen (14), all five CSVs, printable report.
   425	
   426	**Spec Phase 4 — Nice-to-haves**
   427	- Member push notifications.
   428	- Extra reports.
   429	- Skedda history import.
   430	- Optional "hide my name on the studio tablet".
   431	
   432	Each phase ships to staff for testing before members see it.
   433	
   434	---
   435	
   436	## 16. Out of scope (don't build)
   437	
   438	- Two-way messaging or chat.
   439	- Comments on posts.
   440	- Any email from the app other than Firebase sign-in links.
   441	- Booking a specific station or wheel.
   442	- Showing other members' names anywhere **except** the in-studio kiosk list and the same-last-4 tie-break (#45).
   443	- Live kiln status tracking.
   444	- In-app pause or cancellation requests (members email instead).
   445	- Payments.
   446	- An RSVP or "remind me" on recurring events.
   447	- A separate standing-wheel category.
   448	- Writing anything back to Membership Manager (#37).
   449	- Recurring bookings ("every Tuesday 6–9"). Members book each session individually (#55).

