   308	
   309	## 11. Reports (14, in `/staff`; staff with the `my-clay-hub` box, managers and admins) (#50)
   310	
   311	- **Filters:** date range (Last 30 days / This month / Last 6 months / **All time** / Custom), and area.
   312	- **Summary numbers:** hours booked, hours used (checked in), check-in rate, no-shows, active members.
   313	- **"When the studio is busy" heatmap:** days of the week × hours from 5 AM to closing, showing the average number of people checked in.
   314	- **By area:** % booked; how often the area was at or over capacity (the count is shown even when over); how many "pretty full" warnings were shown, and how many members then switched area or time; sessions extended.
   315	- **Member table:** searchable. Columns: booked, used, check-in rate, no-shows, extended, average per week.
   316	- **Member detail panel:** a range picker (8 weeks / 6 months / **All time**); weekly bars against the 20-hr cap (weeks at the cap highlighted); usual area; usual time; check-in rate; member since; lifetime hours; **Export this member's history**.
   317	- **Downloads (CSV), all respecting the filters:**
   318	  1. **Full activity log:** every event, one row each, timestamped.
   319	  2. **Hourly occupancy:** the heatmap's raw data (date, hour, area, people checked in, spots booked).
   320	  3. **Member summary:** one row per member.
   321	  4. **Area summary:** one row per area per day.
   322	  5. **Events & RSVPs:** RSVPs vs attendance.
   323	- **Printable report:** a print-friendly page of the overview. This replaces the manual Skedda review.
   324	
   325	**Later reports (Phase 4+)**, all computed from the same activity log:
   326	- late-night (10–11 PM) and early (5–7 AM) usage, as input to the midnight and 5 AM decisions
   327	- demand vs capacity, by area and time
   328	- weekly cap pressure: how many members hit 20 hours, and how often
   329	- a drop-off list: members with no booking in 3+ weeks
   330	- app adoption: signed in, push enabled
   331	- event RSVP vs attendance trends
   332	- cancellation lead time
   333	- no-show alerts: how often staff found the person was actually there
   334	
   335	---
   336	
   337	## 12. Activity log (build first, keep forever)
   338	
   339	Every booking-related action is written as its **own immutable, timestamped record**. The booking is never simply overwritten. Record types:
   340	- booking created
   341	- cancelled (with who or what: member, pause, offboarding)
   342	- checked in (with the method: qr / kiosk / app / staff)
   343	- started early ("Start now", with the mode)
   344	- extended (with minutes)
   345	- checked out (with the reason: auto_end / early / wrapping_up)
   346	- released (no-show)
   347	- no-show alert sent (and how staff resolved it)
   348	- RSVP added or removed
   349	- event attendance marked
   350	
   351	Reports and CSVs are computed from this log. Nothing is ever deleted from it.
   352	
   353	**[Optional, Phase 4]** Import past Skedda exports into the log, so "All time" really is all time.
   354	
   355	---
   356	
   357	## 13. Security and privacy (non-negotiable)
   358	
   359	- **Members never get an account in `tinker-hq-apps`.** My Clay Hub is its own Firebase project, with its own rules. The only connection is the one-way link, which can read Membership Manager's records and can do nothing in My Clay Hub except call one private function (#30, #42).
   360	- Members can read **only their own** member fields, and **only their own** bookings, inbox and RSVPs.
   361	- Every member rule checks the member's **live status**, not just their sign-in claim. A pause or offboarding takes effect immediately (#33).
   362	- Capacity counts and RSVP counts are shown **without exposing who booked**. They're served from server-maintained aggregate docs or a Cloud Function. Clients can never query other members' bookings.
   363	- **No member ever sees another member's name in the app.** There are two exceptions, both on the in-studio kiosk:
   364	  - the same-last-4 tie-break (first name and last initial);
   365	  - the "Here now / Arriving soon" first-name list (#45).
   366	- **Full phone numbers never reach My Clay Hub.** Only the last 4 digits are copied (#24). No client can read them. Kiosk lookups go through a function that returns only candidate first name, last initial and booking status.
   367	- Staff screens are gated by the staff roster (from Manage Team) in both the UI and the Firestore rules, checked live.
   368	- Write **Firestore rules tests** (emulator) for every rule above before Phase 1 ships. The first test is "a signed-in stranger can do nothing".
   369	
   370	---
   371	
   372	## 14. Time-based jobs
   373	
   374	All of these run on the server (2nd-gen Cloud Functions, or Cloud Tasks), with **retries explicitly switched on**. They must be **idempotent**, meaning safe to run twice:
   375	- check-in reminder (+10 min), last call (+20 min, **plus the staff no-show alert**), release (+30 min)
   376	- still here? (end − 10 min), auto check-out at the end
   377	- closing-time wrap-up message
   378	- event-day reminder
   379	- pause set → cancel bookings in the pause window
   380	- offboarding: disable sign-in and cancel future bookings, from the day after the last day
   381	- member-status recompute: daily at **09:30 UTC** — 3:30 AM MDT / 2:30 AM MST, always after Denver midnight and before opening (#65)
   382	- the link's reconcile: every 6 hours
   383	- inbox TTL cleanup (a Firestore TTL policy)
   384	
   385	All member-facing times and calendar days are **America/Denver**. Scheduled jobs are *declared* in UTC (the functions guard allows only UTC), at times chosen to land in the right Denver window all year (#65). The tests must cover **DST changes** and **week boundaries**, for example a Sunday booking ending at 12:00 AM counts in that Sunday's week. No booking can cross midnight (DATA-MODEL.md, C6).
   386	
   387	`tinker-hq-apps` is on the **Blaze** plan. `my-clay-hub` will be created on Blaze in plan Phase D. Each project records its Firestore location, trigger location and function region (#54).
   388	
   389	---
   390	
   391	## 15. Build phases
   392	
   393	The foundation plan (`clayhub-members-foundation.html`) runs its own phases A–E first. This spec's phases map onto it like this:
   394	
   395	**Spec Phase 0 — Inspect and confirm (no app code): done.** This was plan Phase C, Sep 27, 2026. The existing systems were inspected, every open item was answered, and these docs were rewritten.
   396	
   397	**Before Phase 1 (plan phases A, B, D, D2, E):**
   398	- retire Clay Hub Booking;
   399	- make Membership Manager's saves reliable, fix its dates, and add a permanent member ID;
   400	- create the `my-clay-hub` project;
   401	- build a deploy guard for functions;
   402	- build the one-way link.
   403	
   404	**Spec Phase 1 — Book and check in (launch core); plan Phase F, its own plan:**
   405	- The Tinker HQ tile and Manage Team box; sign-in switched on (only now).
   406	- Member sign-in gated by membership status (§2, §3); paused, review and offboarded handling.
   407	- The staff login exchange; the minimal `/staff` Today view (today's bookings, who's checked in) with **no-show alerts and staff push**.
   408	- Settings: areas, capacities, hours, cap, timings.
   409	- Book (05/06) with soft capacity, the hard weekly cap, 15-minute times and the 14-day window.
   410	- My time (08).
   411	- Check-in: app, QR deep link, "Start now", and the kiosk tablet (13), including walk-in booking and the "Here now / Arriving soon" list.
   412	- Reminder → last call → release (03/04).
   413	- "Still here?" and extensions (11); auto check-out; check out early (10).
   414	- **Activity log.** Inbox (in-app). Profile (09).
   415	- Tests: hours math, capacity counts, lifecycle transitions, status derivation, time-zone and DST cases, Firestore rules.
   416	
   417	**Spec Phase 2 — Community**
   418	- Feed with posts, photos, and Love it (02).
   419	- Staff composer (12).
   420	- What's on (07): recurring listings (with semester dates), one-off events and RSVPs, Changes and the Feed banner, reminders, pot icons (mockups shown to Christie first).
   421	- Staff Events screen (15).
   422	
   423	**Spec Phase 3 — Reports**
   424	- Reports screen (14), all five CSVs, printable report.
   425	
   426	**Spec Phase 4 — Nice-to-haves**
   427	- Member push notifications.
   428	- Extra reports.
   429	- Skedda history import.
   430	- Optional "hide my name on the studio tablet".

