     1	# Data model (Firestore)
     2	
     3	Decided in the foundation plan (`~/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html`) after inspecting the
     4	real Membership Manager and Tinker HQ code (Sep 25–27, 2026). The decision numbers (#30…) refer to `DECISIONS.md`. Collection
     5	and field names here are the plan of record. Change them only through a new decision.
     6	
     7	## Two Firebase projects (#30)
     8	
     9	| Project | Who signs in | What lives here |
    10	|---|---|---|
    11	| `tinker-hq-apps` | Staff only (email/password) | Every internal Tinker app, including **Membership Manager** (`clayHub_members`) and Tinker HQ (`users`). My Clay Hub adds **nothing** here except the `clayhub-link` functions. |
    12	| `my-clay-hub` | Members (magic link, Google), staff via `/staff` (exchanged Tinker HQ login), the kiosk account | Everything below. Its own rules (`my-clay-hub/firestore.rules`), its own guard. |
    13	
    14	Nothing in `my-clay-hub` can read or write `tinker-hq-apps`. Members never get an account in `tinker-hq-apps`.
    15	
    16	## Where member data comes from (source, read-only)
    17	
    18	`tinker-hq-apps` → `clayHub_members/{docId}`. This is Membership Manager's collection, and it's **never written by this app** (#37).
    19	
    20	- **Doc ID:** the email lowercased, with `.` and `/` replaced by `_`. It isn't unique (`a.b@x.com` and `a_b@x.com` collide), so it's never used as an identity.
    21	- **`memberId`:** a permanent random ID, added by Membership Manager in plan Phase B (#52). **This is the identity everywhere in My Clay Hub.**
    22	- **`retired: true`:** set on the old doc when staff change a member's email (Phase B). Live means `retired !== true`.
    23	- **`name`:** one string (there's no first/last split). **`email`:** original case. **`phone`:** free text (blank for some Sawyer imports).
    24	- **`stage`:** `onboarding | touring | active | paused | offboarding | cancelled`. It's only brought up to date when someone opens Membership Manager.
    25	- **Pause dates**, in `YYYY-MM-DD` strings:
    26	  - `scheduledPause.startDate` / `.endDate`;
    27	  - `pauseHistory[]` entries, which use **either** `startDate`/`endDate` **or** the legacy `start`/`end`.
    28	- **Last day:** `scheduledCancellation.finalAccessDate` (`YYYY-MM-DD`).
    29	- **`memberSince`:** added in Phase B (#36).
    30	
    31	`tinker-hq-apps` → `users/{uid}` (Tinker HQ staff): `role`, `appAccess[]`, `active`. Read by the link to build the staff roster.
    32	
    33	## The one-way link (#53)
    34	
    35	1. A 2nd-gen trigger in `tinker-hq-apps` (`clayhub-link`) fires when a `clayHub_members` doc changes. It collects the `memberId` from the before **and** after versions.
    36	2. For each `memberId`, it runs **one query filtered on `memberId` only**, and decides live/retired in memory. The query's `readTime` is the snapshot time.
    37	   - exactly one live doc → a snapshot of that doc's allowed fields;
    38	   - no live doc → a tombstone;
    39	   - **more than one live doc → a conflict:** nothing is sent, and it alerts.
    40	3. It POSTs the envelope (below) to the private HTTPS function `ingestMemberUpdate` in `my-clay-hub`, using its own service account's identity token. Only 200, 400 and 409 answers are final; anything else throws, so the trigger is retried.
    41	4. `ingestMemberUpdate`, in a transaction:
    42	   - rejects the payload unless it's strictly valid;
    43	   - **ignores it unless `readTime` is later than the stored `sourceReadTime`** (a member with no stored time accepts anything), comparing seconds *and* nanoseconds; an accepted envelope always advances `sourceReadTime`, even when nothing else changed;
    44	   - runs `deriveStatus`, and writes `members/{memberId}` and `memberProfiles/{memberId}` together;
    45	   - **never deletes**; a removal replaces the doc with a removed record (#71).
    46	
    47	- **Staff roster:** `users/{uid}` changes flow the same way into `staffRoster/staff_{uid}`, using that document read's `readTime`. Only people with an explicit grant are sent: `role` exactly `admin`|`manager`|`staff`, `active` absent or `true`, `appAccess` absent or a list of strings, and a manager or admin role or `appAccess` containing `my-clay-hub` (#68). Anything else, including a malformed doc, becomes a removal (malformed also alerts, naming the uid only); a removal for someone never held writes nothing.
    48	- **Reconcile:** every 6 hours (01:15, 07:15, 13:15, 19:15 UTC). It reads the whole source in **one read-only transaction pinned to a single `readTime`**, then sends the complete set in one `reconcile` envelope per scope; `ingestMemberUpdate` works out every change and applies it in **one transaction**, or nothing.
    49	  - If the read is incomplete, or a live member doc has no valid `memberId`, it sends nothing and alerts.
    50	  - A `memberId` with more than one live doc is sent as **held**: neither updated nor removed.
    51	  - A record newer than the batch (a trigger landed meanwhile) is never removed.
    52	  - The safety stops (#72) apply — denominators exclude held ids, additions never count, a removal counts only as a removal — and a stop writes nothing, answers 409 and logs the counts and ids.
    53	- `sourceReadTime` is a `tinker-hq-apps` timestamp. It's only ever compared with other `tinker-hq-apps` read times.
    54	
    55	**Copied fields only** — rebuilt from allowed keys at every level, never copied and trimmed: `name`, `email` (strings, else `null`), `emailLower` (`email` lowercased, or `null`), `memberSince` (a valid date, else `null`), `stage` (a known stage, else `"!malformed"`), `retired` (only `true`), `scheduledPause` (`null`, `{startDate, endDate, processed}`, or `"!malformed"` if not an object; `processed` is `true` only when the source `scheduledAt` is present and non-empty), `pauseHistory` (`[]`, a list of `{startDate, endDate, priorTerm?}` entries — legacy `start`/`end` mapped, the modern value winning — with `"!malformed"` for an entry that isn't an object, or `"!malformed"` if it isn't a list), `scheduledCancellation` (`null`, `{finalAccessDate}`, or `"!malformed"`), and **`phoneLast4`**, worked out in `tinker-hq-apps` with Membership Manager's own phone rule (10 digits, or 11 starting with 1; else `null`). Every date is a valid `YYYY-MM-DD`, absent, or `"!malformed"` — never raw text. `firstName` and `lastInitial` are worked out on receipt. The full phone number never leaves that project (#24).
    56	
    57	**Never copied, at any nesting level:** `keypadCode`, `keypadUserId`, `staffNotes`, `notes` (including the notes inside pause and cancellation entries), `application`, `actions`, the full phone, the shelf fields, billing and Sawyer fields (`lastBilling`, `processDate`, `sawyerProcessedAt`, …), audit timestamps (`scheduledAt` is reduced to the `processed` flag), and anything not listed above.
    58	
    59	**The envelope (summary; the exact contract is the Phase E plan's "The link contract", and E-1 adds a fixture set both repos test against):** `{v:1, kind: 'member'|'staff'|'reconcile', readTime: {seconds: "<decimal string>", nanos: <int 0..999999999>}, …}`.
    60	- Any unknown key, version or kind, a non-canonical `readTime`, a `memberId` not matching Membership Manager's `m_` + version-4 UUID pattern, or duplicate ids in a reconcile → **400**, nothing written.
    61	- Answers: 200 `{result: applied|unchanged|stale}`, 400, or 409 (a stopped reconcile). `updatedAt` moves only when content changes; `sourceReadTime` advances on every accepted envelope.
    62	- Logs never contain names, emails, phone digits, notes or source documents.
    63	
    64	## `deriveStatus(source, todayDenver)` (#34, #35)
    65	
    66	Code: `shared/derive-status.js`, using `shared/denver-time.js`. These are the only status and date code: `ingestMemberUpdate` and
    67	the daily recompute (09:30 UTC, #65) import them, and nothing re-derives status elsewhere. `todayDenver` is passed in, never read from the clock inside.
    68	
    69	Denver calendar dates only. `YYYY-MM-DD` strings are compared as dates, never through `new Date()`. A date must be strictly
    70	`YYYY-MM-DD` and a real day (no `2026-02-30`, no other shapes); anything else is **malformed**. The rules below run in order; the first match wins.
    71	
    72	1. No live source record (tombstone) → **`removed`**
    73	2. `stage` is `onboarding` or `touring` → **`not_yet`**
    74	3. `stage` is missing, or isn't one of the six known values → **`review`**
    75	4. `scheduledCancellation.finalAccessDate`:
    76	   - present but malformed → **`review`**;
    77	   - valid, and today is **after** it → **`offboarded`**. The last day itself still has access.
    78	5. `stage: 'cancelled'` with no `finalAccessDate` → **`offboarded`**
    79	6. `stage: 'offboarding'` with no `finalAccessDate` → **`review`**
    80	7. A `scheduledPause` that isn't an object is malformed → **`review`**. A `scheduledPause` object Membership Manager hasn't processed (`processed` isn't `true`) is **ignored** (#70; pause history entries are always processed).
    81	8. Any pause window (in a processed `scheduledPause` or any `pauseHistory` entry, either spelling) that is **missing, malformed, or reversed** (its end is before its start) → **`review`** (C8). A one-day pause (start = end) is valid. A pause with a start but **no end
    82	   date** is `review` too, never "paused indefinitely" (#59): staff see the flag and add the end date, and the pause's booking
    83	   cancellation happens then (a window with no end gives nothing to cancel against).
    84	9. Any valid pause window with **start ≤ today ≤ end** (both days included) → **`paused`**
    85	10. `stage: 'paused'` with no pause windows at all → **`review`**
    86	11. Otherwise → **`active`**. That covers `active`, a paused stage whose window has ended, `offboarding` before the last day, and `cancelled` with a future last day.
    87	
    88	How the code reads the edges of these rules (D-5):
    89	- Rule 1 also treats a record with `retired: true` as no live record, since live means `retired !== true`.
    90	- A cleared pause or cancellation is `null` in Membership Manager, and counts as absent. A `scheduledCancellation` without a
    91	  `finalAccessDate` (`null` or missing) means no last day. Any other `finalAccessDate`, **including an empty string**, must be a
    92	  valid date or it's malformed (rule 4 → `review`).
    93	- A pause entry uses `startDate`/`endDate` when they're set, else the legacy `start`/`end`.
    94	- A source that isn't a record at all gives `review`. `deriveStatus` never throws on member data; it throws only if `todayDenver`
    95	  itself isn't a valid date (a caller bug). Supported dates are 1900–2999.
    96	- **Input shape:** `deriveStatus` reads the `clayHub_members` field shape (`stage`, `scheduledPause`, `pauseHistory`,
    97	  `scheduledCancellation.finalAccessDate`, plus `tombstone`/`retired`). Whatever `members/*` stores, `ingestMemberUpdate` and the daily recompute must
    98	  hand it that shape — **including `tombstone: true` for a removed record**, which keeps its stage and dates (#71) and would
    99	  otherwise read as active or paused. A flattened record would silently read as "no pause, no last day". Phase E tests that round trip.
   100	- **Deliberate differences from Membership Manager**, where it reads the same fields differently:
   101	  - A missing `stage` is `review` here (rule 3). Membership Manager treats it as active.
   102	  - Waitlisted and deferred people are stored as `stage: 'cancelled'`, so they derive to `offboarded`, not `not_yet`. Neither
   103	    can sign in, so the outcome is the same; it means `offboarded` isn't only former members.
   104	- As a check, run against the Sep 28, 2026 backup of all 66 `clayHub_members` records: every date was strict `YYYY-MM-DD`, and
   105	  none came out as `review`.
   106	
   107	| Status | Can sign in | Can book | Notes |
   108	|---|---|---|---|
   109	| `active` | yes | yes | |
   110	| `paused` | yes | no | Feed, What's on and My time are visible. The paused message names the day booking reopens (end + 1). |
   111	| `review` | yes | no | "We're checking your membership details — you can still see the feed." Staff see a flag. |
   112	| `offboarded`, `not_yet`, `removed` | no | no | `enforceMemberStatus` removes the claim, revokes sessions, and disables offboarded accounts (never deletes them). |
   113	
   114	It runs inside `ingestMemberUpdate` on every write, and again for everyone daily at **09:30 UTC** (#65), for that day's Denver date. The recompute is one transaction; it rewrites `status`, `statusDate` and the profile's `status`/`pause` (and `updatedAt` only when content changes), and stops on more unexplained changes than #72 allows. Since #70 (Oct 8) inserted rule 7, rules 8–11 were numbered 7–10 before; older DECISIONS rows use the old numbers.
   115	
   116	## Collections in `my-clay-hub`
   117	
   118	`members/{memberId}`: the projection. It's written **only** by `ingestMemberUpdate` and, for `status`/`statusDate` only, the daily recompute (both as `ingest@`, never deleting).
   119	- The copied fields above, plus `memberId`, `firstName`, `lastInitial`, `status`, `statusDate` (the Denver date it was derived for), `sourceReadTime`, `tombstone`, `updatedAt`.
   120	- **A removed member (#71)** keeps the last stored snapshot fields **minus `email`, `emailLower` and `phoneLast4`**, plus `{memberId, firstName, lastInitial, tombstone: true, status: 'removed', statusDate, sourceReadTime, updatedAt}`; if nothing was ever stored for that `memberId`, only those last fields. A later live record replaces it with the full allowlist again.
   121	- **No client can read it**, not even the member themselves: Firestore rules can't hide single fields, and it holds `phoneLast4` (#24). Functions and rules read it on the server.
   122	
   123	`memberProfiles/{memberId}`: the **member-readable view**, written by `ingestMemberUpdate` alongside `members` (and its `status`/`pause` by the daily recompute). Exactly `memberId`, `firstName`, `name`, `email`, `status`, `memberSince`, `pause` (the valid, processed window containing today, else the earliest one starting after today, else `null`), `finalAccessDate` (only if valid), `updatedAt`. **Never `phoneLast4`, never a malformed marker.** A removed member's profile is just `{memberId, tombstone: true, status: 'removed', updatedAt}`. A member can read only their own (from Phase F; deny-all until then).
   124	
   125	`staffRoster/staff_{uid}`: `{ uid, name, role, sourceReadTime, updatedAt, tombstone }` for granted staff only (#68), written only by `ingestMemberUpdate`; a removal leaves `{ uid, tombstone: true, sourceReadTime, updatedAt }`. **No client can read it**; rules and functions check it.
   126	
   127	`linkOverrides/{id}`: single-use, scoped, expiring overrides for the safety stops (#72), created only by Christie in the Console. Exact keys per scope (`members`: `maxStatusChanges?`, `maxRemovals?`; `staff`: `maxRemovals`; `recompute`: `maxStatusChanges`), plus `scope`, `expiresAt` (no more than 24 h after the doc's Firestore `createTime`) and `usedAt` (`null`; a server timestamp once used). Limits are integers 0–249; `members` needs at least one, and an omitted one keeps its normal value. An override is used only when the normal limit would stop the run, and is consumed in the same transaction; two eligible overrides for one scope → both refused. The exact rules are in the Phase E plan (E-2). **Deny-all for every client, permanently.**
   128	
   129	`settings/app`: a single doc, editable by managers and admins (#50).
   130	- `areas`: `[{ id: 'glaze', name: 'Glaze station', capacity: 4 }, { id: 'wheels', name: 'Wheels', capacity: 10 }, { id: 'handbuilding', name: 'Handbuilding table', capacity: 6 }]`. The 10 wheels include the 2 standing wheels, which aren't a separate area (#8).
   131	- `openTime: '05:00'`; `closeTimes: { mon…sun: '23:00' }`. Tuesday is locked at 23:00; the others can be set to 24:00 later (#27).
   132	- `weeklyCapHours: 20`, where the week runs from Mon 00:00 to the next Mon 00:00, America/Denver (C6).
   133	- `bookAheadDays: 14` (#49)
   134	- `startStepMinutes: 15`; `lengthChipsHours: [1,2,3,4,5,6]`; `maxLengthHours: 6`; `endTimeStepMinutes: 15` (#48)
   135	- `earlyCheckoutRefund: { stepMinutes: 15, rounding: 'up' }` (#48)
   136	- `timing: { checkInOpensBeforeMin: 15, reminderMin: 10, lastCallMin: 20, releaseMin: 30, stillHereBeforeEndMin: 10 }`
   137	- `extensionOptionsMin: [30, 60, 90, 120]`
   138	- `kilns: [{ name: 'Hestia' }, { name: 'Lumi' }]`
   139	- `links: { askClayHub: 'https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd-RhLmSXsrlzow3JK7m0H77pEp3Gg5_zo0eKxNBBru1v0QoA/viewform', membershipEmail: 'clayhub@tinkerartstudio.com' }`
   140	- `timezone: 'America/Denver'`
   141	
   142	`bookings/{bookingId}`
   143	- `memberId`, `areaId`
   144	- `start`, `end`: Timestamps on 15-minute boundaries. `end` moves later on an extension. "Start now" always moves `start` earlier; with `same_length`, `end` moves earlier by the same amount, and with `keep_end`, `end` stays.
   145	- `status`: `booked | checked_in | checked_out | cancelled | released`
   146	- `checkedInAt`, `checkInMethod`: `qr | kiosk | app | staff` (staff = "They're here", #46)
   147	- `checkedOutAt`, `checkOutReason`: `auto_end | early | wrapping_up`
   148	- `startedEarly?`: `{ mode: 'same_length' | 'keep_end', originalStart }` (#47)
   149	- `weekKey` (e.g. `'2026-W39'`, the Mon–Sun week in Denver). **ISO-8601**, with the ISO week-year and a two-digit week (C7):
   150	  `2026-W09`; 2027-01-01 is in `2026-W53`, and 2027-01-04 starts `2027-W01`. Worked out only by `isoWeekKey` in `shared/denver-time.js`.
   151	- `minutesCounted`: what this booking counts toward the cap, in minutes
   152	- **Invariant: every booking belongs wholly to its start date's week** (C6). A booking is the half-open span `[start, end)`,
   153	  and no booked minute is at or after that day's closing time. An end of 12:00 AM is stored as the next day's 00:00 but adds
   154	  no minutes to that day: a Sunday 10 PM – 12:00 AM booking is 120 minutes in that Sunday's week and none in Monday's.
   155	  `bookingWeek` in `shared/denver-time.js` reports a booking with any minute in the next day as **malformed** (no `weekKey`),
   156	  never quietly giving it the start week. Phase F's settings must reject a closing time later than 12:00 AM (SPEC §4 and §5
   157	  already rule out anything overnight).
   158	- `createdAt`, `createdVia`: `app | kiosk | staff`
   159	- Readable by the owner and staff only.
   160	
   161	`weeklyHours/{memberId}_{weekKey}`: server-maintained `{ bookedMinutes }`, used by the meter and the cap checks. It's recomputed from bookings in tests.
   162	
   163	`occupancy/{areaId}_{date}_{HHMM}`: server-maintained counts **per 15-minute slot**, `{ booked, checkedIn }`. This is how members see capacity without seeing each other's bookings. The busy-times heatmap rolls these up to hours.
   164	
   165	`activityLog/{eventId}`: **immutable, never deleted** (#26).
   166	- `type`: `booking_created | cancelled | checked_in | started_early | extended | checked_out | released | no_show_alerted | rsvp_added | rsvp_removed | attendance_marked`
   167	- `memberId`, `bookingId` / `eventId`, `areaId`, `at`
   168	- `actor`: `member | kiosk | system | staff:{staffUid}`
   169	- `details`: `{ method, reason, minutes, cancelledBy, … }`
   170	- Staff with reports access can read it; only the server writes.
   171	
   172	`inbox/{memberId}/items/{itemId}`
   173	- `type`, `title`, `body`, `createdAt`, `readAt`
   174	- `expiresAt` (a TTL, 14 days)
   175	- `bookingId?` and `stage?` (`reminder | last_call | released`), so the card updates in place
   176	- `actions?`
   177	
   178	`staffAlerts/{alertId}`: no-show alerts (#46): `{ bookingId, memberId, firstName, lastInitial, areaId, start, createdAt, resolution: null | 'checked_in' | 'not_here' }`. Staff can read it.
   179	
   180	`staffPush/{staffUid}`: web-push subscriptions for staff phones (#46). Written by the owning staff session, read by the server.
   181	
   182	`posts/{postId}`
   183	- `type`: `firing_photos | studio_update`
   184	- `text`, `photos[]` (Storage paths)
   185	- `authorName`, `createdAt`, `notify`, `loveCount`
   186	- `posts/{postId}/loves/{memberId}` holds each member's love, and is never exposed as a list.
   187	
   188	`changes/{changeId}`: schedule-change alerts. `title`, `body`, `kind` (`cancelled | moved | closed | other`), `startsAt`, `endsAt` (unpins automatically), `relatedEventId?` / `occurrenceDate?`, `createdBy`.
   189	
   190	`events/{eventId}`
   191	- `kind`: `recurring_listed | one_off_rsvp`
   192	- `title`, `description`
   193	- `icon`: a pot illustration key (#51)
   194	- For recurring events: `weekday` + `startTime` / `endTime`, and optional **`activeFrom` / `activeUntil`**, so each semester's Office Hours swap over automatically. For one-off events: `start` / `end`.
   195	- `rsvpEnabled`, `cap?`, `cancelledDates[]` (recurring)
   196	- `events/{eventId}/rsvps/{memberId}`: `{ going, updatedAt }`. Members read and write their own; the count is served by a server-maintained `goingCount`.
   197	- `events/{eventId}/attendance/{memberId}`: marked by staff after the event.
   198	
   199	`reminders/{id}`: the standing reminder lines for What's on, managed by staff.
   200	
   201	## Server functions
   202	
   203	**In `tinker-hq-apps`** (codebase `clayhub-link`: read-only there, and it can only invoke `ingestMemberUpdate`):
   204	- `onClayHubMemberWritten`, `onStaffUserWritten`: re-read the source and send a snapshot.
   205	- `reconcileLink`: every 6 hours, as above.
   206	- The two **trigger** services (`onclayhubmemberwritten`, `onstaffuserwritten`) get `run.invoker` for `clayhub-link@` from Christie's recorded grant on exactly those two services, never project-wide; the guard declares and attests that list (#73). (Project Owners can always invoke; Google's project-wide grant to the default Compute account is removed after the first release and its removal proven, #67.)
   207	
   208	**In `my-clay-hub`:**
   209	- `ingestMemberUpdate`: private HTTPS; its only invoker is `clayhub-link@tinker-hq-apps`. The writer of `members`, `memberProfiles` and `staffRoster`. Runs `deriveStatus`. Can't delete.
   210	- `recomputeStatuses`: daily at 09:30 UTC (#65); one transaction; writes only `status`, `statusDate` and the profile's `status`/`pause`.
   211	- `claimMembership`: callable after sign-in. Uses the verified email only; exactly one live, sign-in-eligible member; sets `member: {memberId}` (#33).
   212	- `exchangeStaffSession`: verifies the Tinker HQ ID token, checks `staffRoster/staff_{uid}`, then getUser/createUser → claims → custom token (#31).
   213	- `enforceMemberStatus`: removes claims, revokes sessions, and disables accounts for `offboarded`, `not_yet` and `removed`.
   214	- `onMemberStatusChange`: a trigger on `members/{memberId}` in `my-clay-hub` that fires when `status` or a pause window changes.
   215	  - A new or changed pause window cancels that member's bookings inside the window.
   216	  - `offboarded` cancels all their future bookings.
   217	  - Each cancellation writes an inbox notice and an activity-log entry. It's idempotent.
   218	- `onBookingWrite`: validates the cap, maintains `weeklyHours` and `occupancy`, writes to `activityLog`.
   219	- `scheduledTicker` (or per-booking Cloud Tasks): reminder (+10), last call (+20, plus the staff no-show alert and push), release (+30), "Still here?" (end −10), auto check-out, the closing-time message, and event-day reminders. All idempotent.
   220	- `kioskLookup(last4)`: kiosk role only. Returns candidates `{ memberId, firstName, lastInitial, bookingNow? }` (#24).
   221	- `kioskNowList`: kiosk role only. The "Here now / Arriving soon" first-name list (#45).
   222	- `exportCsv(type, filters)`: staff with reports access only (#50).
   223	
   224	All scheduled jobs are 2nd gen, with explicit retries, **declared in UTC** (the guard allows only UTC; #65) at times that land in the right Denver window all year; what they compute uses Denver calendar days, and is tested for DST changes and week boundaries.

