    31	| 21 | One-off events use **"I'm in"**, which doesn't count toward hours, and RSVPers are notified about changes | Lets staff reach exactly the people who planned to come. | — |
    32	| 22 | Pause and cancel requests go by **email** to clayhub@tinkerartstudio.com, and questions go to the **Ask Clay Hub** Google Form (link out) | Simplest option that works. No request flow to build or debug. | An in-app request form. |
    33	| 23 | **SUPERSEDED Sep 27 by #53.** ~~Membership Manager is the single source of truth, read directly, with no synced copy.~~ Membership Manager is **still** the single source of truth, and status still drives access automatically. But member data now reaches My Clay Hub through a **one-way projection** into its own project, because My Clay Hub lives in a separate Firebase project (#30). | Staff never update two systems (unchanged). | Syncing a separate copy of member data (now chosen, one-way only, because of #30). |
